{#
  Renders from content/alg2/* (docs/CONTENT_MODEL.md) instead of the legacy
  {% include "tracks/alg2.html" %} — fifteenth track cut over, following the established pattern
  (docs/DECISIONS/0005-qudrat-cutover.md through 0015). index.html (deleted, WP10 step 4 — docs/DECISIONS/0023; still recoverable via
  git history) and src/_includes/tracks/alg2.html (also deleted, same step) used
  to be kept as an inert rollback path — no longer needed once every track had been
  migrated and verified live.

  Notes (WP27): chapterTag is the 'category' variant reused with new className/badgeClassName
  ("a2-tag"/"a2-paper") and a non-percentage weightBadge ("A2" — the field just holds a string,
  no format assumed). No orphaned-content bug, no markup corruption this time. hasFullExam:false
  like geo (no "Full official exam paper" section in source at all).

  Two new real explorer-control shapes (docs/DECISIONS/0016):
  - controls[].options[].selected — polyDeg's <select> DOES mark one <option selected> explicitly
    (unlike apab's apRiemType, which had none) — the option value differs per real instance, so
    'selected' had to become per-item, not assumed either way.
  - controls[].valueDisplay — polyA's <input value="2"> but its <span> shows "1": engine.js maps
    slider positions to a different displayed scale. Real, confirmed byte-for-byte in source, not
    a typo — added a field for when the display text differs from the input's own value attribute.
  Also: readouts[] can now legitimately be an empty array (a2-conics' explorer has select+range
  controls and a live-equation note, but literally no .readout div at all) — already schema-legal,
  first real instance seen.

  Found and FIXED a real LaTeX-escaping bug in a2-matrices' "Solving a 3×3 system" worked example:
  source is missing \\ row-separators inside \begin{pmatrix}...\end{pmatrix} (e.g. "2&1\1&-3"
  instead of "2&1\\1&-3"), which would throw a KaTeX parse error on the live page. Fixed by
  restoring the missing backslashes; every other character preserved verbatim. docs/DECISIONS/0016.
#}
